# The Foundation Piles - the tenth island of the library's plan The City That Never Sank (SL13, Highwater, chapter 9, the
# finale's second part)
# Under the city: a forest of giant stone piles standing in a basin ten metres down, two of them cracked and leaning,
# shoring jacks at the feet of four, air trapped round their foot-blocks; a stingray grown huge nests among them. At the
# city's edge a mudflat lies dry at sea level, with the pile engineer's hut, clay and sand, and something buried. Quest
# "The Piles" (12 steps): the mudflat, the engineer's note, the first two piles and their jacks, the pile stingray in two
# phases, the last two jacks, the closing note, back to the mudflat.
#
# Points: the mudflat 24 0 (levelled at 0.8, r 12); the pile basin -16 0 (levelled at -10, r 22); piles at -24 -12
# (pile 1), -8 -12 (pile 2), -8 12 (pile 3), -24 12 (pile 4), more piles between; the jacks 3 m east of each pile;
# the air pockets beside the jacks; the stingray's nest -16 0; the treasure within 10 of 18 0.
include lib_sea
include lib_rt
include lib_huts
include lib_features
include lib_verdance
include lib_concord
include lib_highwater
new
gen Trees=0 Bushes=0.1 Rocks=0.4 Harvest=0.1 BeachThings=0.4
gen Seed=13951 Radius=52 Height=2 Roughness=0.2 Peaks=0 Shape=0 Style=0 PeakShape=0.2 Cliffs=0 BeachWidth=0.9
gen Water=0.6 SeaRocks=0.5 SeaFinds=0.5 Sunken=0.5 Hostiles=0 Friendly=0 SeaLife=0.4
generate

# --- Terrain: the mudflat dry, the pile basin deep ------------------------------------------------------------------
brush flatten at 24 0 r=12 s=20 frames=300 h=0.8
brush flatten at -16 0 r=22 s=20 frames=500 h=-10
origin
clear at 24 0 r=12
clear at -16 0 r=23

# --- The storm, still blowing over the city's edge -------------------------------------------------------------------
call weather x=0 z=0 al=storm r=70 fog=#3a4048 fa=0.4 light=#8a96a2 la=0.3 parts=mist h=3
place Zone_Sound stormsound at 0 0 ground y=3

# --- The mudflat: the engineer's hut, his note, clay and sand ---------------------------------------------------------
push at 26 2 h=0.8
call stilt_hut y=2.6 w4=ReefHuts_PlasticWall4
place Loot_ChestSmall engineerbox at 2.25 3.5 y=2.7 sit yaw=180
place Placeable_Lantern_Metal - at 1 3.5 y=2.7 drop
pop
place Note_Board enginenote at 22 -3 ground sit yaw=270
place Zone_Trigger mudzone at 22 0 ground y=1.5
place Zone_Trigger returnzone at 28 -6 ground y=1.5
place Note_Sign returnsign at 28.8 -6 ground sit yaw=270
place "Pickup_Landmark_Clay 1" - at 30 -9 ground sit
place "Pickup_Landmark_Clay 2" - at 32 -5 ground sit
place "Pickup_Landmark_Clay 3" - at 18 8 ground sit
place "Pickup_Landmark_Sand" - at 16 -6 ground sit
place "Pickup_Landmark_Sand" - at 20 10 ground sit
place Reef_Barrel2 - at 31 3 ground sit
place Block_Ladder - at 13 0 ground yaw=270 sy=4
call dirt x=18 z=0 r=6 n=3 seed=13952
call treasure x=18 z=0 r=10 n=1 seed=13054
prop treasure13054 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*3

# --- The pile forest: four piles with jacks, eight more without; two cracked and leaning -----------------------------
place RT_Pillar piles at -24 -12 ground scale=3 sy=4 tilt=4
place RT_Pillar piles at -8 -12 ground scale=3 sy=4
place RT_Pillar piles at -8 12 ground scale=3 sy=4 roll=5
place RT_Pillar piles at -24 12 ground scale=3 sy=4
place RT_Pillar piles at -32 0 ground scale=3 sy=4
place RT_Pillar piles at -16 -20 ground scale=3 sy=4
place RT_Pillar piles at -16 20 ground scale=3 sy=4
place RT_Pillar piles at 0 0 ground scale=3 sy=4
place RT_Pillar piles at -32 -18 ground scale=3 sy=4
place RT_Pillar piles at -32 18 ground scale=3 sy=4
place RT_Pillar piles at 0 -18 ground scale=3 sy=4 tilt=-3
place RT_Pillar piles at 0 18 ground scale=3 sy=4
place Block_Foundation - at -24 -12 ground scale=2
place Block_Foundation - at -8 -12 ground scale=2
place Block_Foundation - at -8 12 ground scale=2
place Block_Foundation - at -24 12 ground scale=2
call crank x=-21 z=-12 yaw=90 alias=jack1
call crank x=-5 z=-12 yaw=90 alias=jack2
call crank x=-5 z=12 yaw=90 alias=jack3
call crank x=-21 z=12 yaw=90 alias=jack4
call hw_airpocket x=-21 z=-9.5 id=pile_1 al=pile1air bub=pile1bub msg="The first jacked pile. Air, trapped round its foot-block - and the jack, seized with rust."
call hw_airpocket x=-5 z=-9.5 id=pile_2 al=pile2air bub=pile2bub msg="The second pile. A crack runs up it as wide as your hand."
call hw_airpocket x=-5 z=9.5 id=pile_3 al=pile3air bub=pile3bub
call hw_airpocket x=-21 z=9.5 id=pile_4 al=pile4air bub=pile4bub
place Note_Paper closing at -21 10.5 ground drop
place Creature_Stingray pileray at -16 0 ground y=2
place Creature_PufferFish puffers at -28 -4 ground y=2
call hw_reef x=-12 z=-16 r=3 seed=13953
call hw_reef x=-20 z=16 r=3 seed=13954
place "Pickup_Landmark_Copper 1" - at -30 6 ground sit
place "Pickup_Landmark_Mushroom 2" - at -12 4 ground sit
call shallows x=0 z=0 r=70 deep=6 n=2 seed=13955
call hw_skyline x=-100 z=-80 a=skyline

# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ------------------------------------------------------------------
info title=The Foundation Piles
info author=Custom Islands
info description=Under Highwater: a forest of giant stone piles ten metres down, two of them cracked, shoring jacks at their feet, air round their foot-blocks - and a stingray grown huge among them. A dry mudflat at the city's edge. The last of The City That Never Sank.
island on.arrive=message||A grey mudflat at the city's edge. Beyond it the water goes black - and down there, the piles the whole city stands on.

story jack1|Pile 1 jacked|Bolt|The first pile, shored up.
story jack2|Pile 2 jacked|Bolt|The second pile, shored up.
story jack3|Pile 3 jacked|Bolt|The third pile, shored up.
story jack4|Pile 4 jacked|Bolt|The fourth pile, shored up - the city holds.
story rayhurt|Pile stingray wounded|Bolt|You wounded the stingray that nests among the piles.
story raydown|Pile stingray defeated|Bolt|The pile stingray is dead. The piles are yours to mend.

prop piles tint.color=#6e6a60
prop piles tint.amount=0.5
prop skyline tint.color=#5a6068
prop skyline tint.amount=0.5
prop stormsound sound.event=event:/amb/rain_ocean
prop stormsound sound.volume=0.6
prop stormsound zone.radius=70
prop puffers creature.count=2
prop pileray creature.count=1
prop pileray creature.respawn=0
prop pileray creature.size=3
prop pileray creature.health=10
prop pileray boss.phase=0.5
prop pileray boss.summon=2
prop pileray tint.color=#3c4a40
prop pileray tint.amount=0.6
prop pileray on.phase=give||story:rayhurt*1\nmessage||The stingray thrashes against a pile - and two more come out of the dark to help it.
prop pileray on.defeat=signal||raydown\ngive||story:rayhurt*1\ngive||story:raydown*1\nmessage||The great stingray drifts down between the piles and lies still. The last two jacks are clear.
prop closing beh.hidden=1
prop closing obj.name=closing

prop jack1 beh.use=Wind the first pile's jack
prop jack1 if.use=!signal|jack1
prop jack1 on.use=signal||jack1\ngive||story:jack1*1\nsound||event:/raft/radar/lever\nmessage||The jack bites. Above you the pile groans - and stops leaning.
prop jack1 else.use=message||This pile is shored.
prop jack2 beh.use=Wind the second pile's jack
prop jack2 if.use=signal|jack1
prop jack2 on.use=signal||jack2\ngive||story:jack2*1\nsound||event:/raft/radar/lever\nmessage||The second jack bites. In the dark between the piles, something big turns toward the sound.
prop jack2 else.use=message||Rusted solid. The engineer's note says: the first pile first.
prop jack3 beh.use=Wind the third pile's jack
prop jack3 if.use=signal|raydown
prop jack3 on.use=signal||jack3\ngive||story:jack3*1\nsound||event:/raft/radar/lever\nmessage||The third pile takes the weight again.
prop jack3 else.use=message||You can't work the jack with that stingray circling.
prop jack4 beh.use=Wind the fourth pile's jack
prop jack4 if.use=signal|jack3
prop jack4 on.use=signal||jack4\ngive||story:jack4*1\nshow|closing\nsound||event:/raft/radar/lever\nmessage||The last jack bites. All through the water the piles settle. Highwater holds - for now. Tucked behind the jack, a note.
prop jack4 else.use=message||The third pile first.

note enginenote Pile engineer's note | THE PILES - ENGINEER'S NOTE\n\nFour piles carry the crown, and the storm has cracked them. The jacks are at their feet, three metres east, where the air collects.\n\nThe first pile first, then the second. Then the far two - if the ray lets you. It has nested down there since the Lowstreet flood.
note engineerbox Engineer's box | The pile engineer's spare tools.
note closing The city holds | Behind the fourth jack, in a tin, the pile engineer's last words -\n\nThe piles are older than the Authority, the Fleet and the Union. They were here before any of them, and they will carry whoever comes after.\n\nThe brass plate on each one: CONCORD WORKS. Whoever built the pumps built this too. Their signal is still out there, south, on the old band.
note returnsign Mudflat | High-water mark. The tide comes no further.
loot engineerbox Rope*2;MetalIngot*2;Bolt*2
prop engineerbox loot.refill=0

prop mudzone zone.id=mudflat
prop mudzone zone.radius=4
prop mudzone zone.message=The mudflat. The engineer's hut, a board, and the black water beyond.
prop returnzone zone.id=mudflat_return
prop returnzone zone.radius=3
prop returnzone zone.message=Back on the mudflat. Up above, the rain is easing off.

quest title=The Piles
quest intro=The storm has cracked the piles under the city. Land on the mudflat at its edge.
step reach|mudflat|1|Land on the mudflat
step read|Pile engineer's note|1|Read the pile engineer's note
step reach|pile_1|1|Dive to the first pile
step collect|story:jack1|1|Wind the first pile's jack
step reach|pile_2|1|Swim to the second pile
step collect|story:jack2|1|Wind the second pile's jack
step collect|story:rayhurt|1|Wound the stingray nesting among the piles
step collect|story:raydown|1|Finish the pile stingray
step collect|story:jack3|1|Wind the third pile's jack
step collect|story:jack4|1|Wind the fourth pile's jack
step read|The city holds|1|Read the note behind the last jack
step reach|mudflat_return|1|Go back up to the mudflat
quest done=Highwater holds. The city that never sank is still standing - and whatever you chose on the Crown, it will have to live with.
quest reward=TitaniumOre*2;TradeToken*10

save The Foundation Piles
